Add an "Assign To..." command to the VS Code extension.

There needs to be a menu item to assign a ticket. Support both predefined names in the config and
free-form text.

Add a `ticketfile.assignees` setting which contains an ordered array of names. It should support
user and workspace configuration in the same way as other array settings. A workspace value should
replace the complete user value. Trim configured names and reject empty or duplicate entries.

The Assign To command should first show configured names, followed by these actions:

- Enter Name... opens a text box for a free-form assignee.
- Clear Assignee removes assignee metadata.

Trim free-form input and reject an empty name. Selecting the current assignee should make no
change. The command should be available from a ticket context menu and the command palette.

Refactor status assignment code into a general metadata-update path where practical. Assignment
must use the selected ticket's full URI, reject changes when the document has unsaved edits, and
preserve ticket-folder ownership. It should add assignment history with wording consistent with
CLI metadata history:

```
assignee set to Clanker.
assignee changed from David Reid to Clanker.
assignee removed (was Clanker).
```

The update and history comment should be written as one operation. Refresh the correct ticket tree
after the write. Missing author configuration should use the existing warning behavior.

